==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{der|fo|non|elska}}, from {{der|fo|gem-pro|*aliskōną||to care for, cultivate, cherish}}, from {{der|fo|gem-pro|*aliskaz||dear, precious}}, from {{der|fo|gem-pro|*al-||to spur, drive, be enthusiastic}}, from {{der|fo|ine-pro|*el-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*lā-||to drive, move, go}}.

===Verb===
{{fo-verb|elskaði|elskaðu|elskað}}

# to [[love]]
#* ''[[eg elski teg|Eg '''elski''' teg]].''
#*: I love you.
#* ''[[antin|Antin]] '''elskar''' [[tú]] [[tað]], [[ella]] [[hata]]r tú tað.''
#*: Either you love it or you hate it.

